#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for the classic confinement review process, including "
"publisher vetting, technical review, and supported use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:8
msgid "Reviewing classic confinement snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:10
msgid "Classic confinement review process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:12
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:13
msgid ""
"As of snapd 2.20, snappy supports `confinement: classic` which allows the "
"snap to run without restrictions. Future releases of snapd will also support "
"a classic interface (name TBD) that operates similarly. Snaps specifying "
"classic confinement may target the stable channel, but are only supported on "
"classic distro systems (ie, not on Ubuntu Core)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:15
msgid ""
"Because classic confinement snaps run without restrictions, use of classic "
"confinement effectively grants device ownership to the snap. Due to the "
"sensitive nature of classic confinement:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:17
msgid ""
"users must specify `--classic` when using `snap install` to install a snap "
"using classic confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:18
msgid ""
"the review process in the snap store will flag for human review snaps that "
"specify classic confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:19
msgid ""
"the store provides a mechanism for the reviewer to allow classic confinement "
"to the snap so that subsequent uploads do not trigger human review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:20
msgid ""
"the publisher shall be vetted using the processes in this topic before "
"classic confinement is granted by the store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:22
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:23
msgid "reviewers are @reviewers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:24
msgid "advocacy team is @advocacy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:25
msgid ""
"classic confinement is defined as `confinement: classic` and the upcoming "
"`classic` interface (final name TBD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:26
msgid ""
"classic confinement applies to a particular snap ID and may be revoked by "
"the store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:28
msgid "Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:29
msgid ""
"the publisher makes the request for classic confinement in the forum using "
"the [store-requests category](https://forum.snapcraft.io/c/store-requests)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:30
msgid ""
"the technical reasons for why the snap uses classic confinement are gathered "
"in the forum post and captured for potential future snapd improvements. The "
"technical requirements will be reviewed by the security team and/or an "
"architect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:31
msgid ""
"the advocacy team, reviewers team and/or architects participate in vetting "
"the snap/publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:32
msgid ""
"once the publisher has been vetted, the technical reasons are captured and "
"the request is approved, a store reviewer will issue a snap declaration for "
"the snap and add a comment to the store, giving the URL to the forum post"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:34
msgid ""
"A template for applying for classic confinement exists [here](https://"
"forum.snapcraft.io/t/about-the-classic-confinement-category/43830)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:36
msgid "Known categories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:38
msgid ""
"Classic requests generally fall under a number of categories. Below lists "
"categories that developers may consult for things that are known to be "
"allowed/disallowed use of classic confinement. @reviewers may consult these "
"lists when processing classic requests. If something falls outside of these "
"lists, then the requirements must be gathered by a senior reviewer and "
"discussed with an architect (after which, it can be added to the lists)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:41
msgid "Supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:42
msgid "compilers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:43
msgid "debug tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:44
msgid "IDEs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:45
msgid "juju helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:46
msgid ""
"kubernetes tools requiring [arbitrary authentication agents](https://"
"forum.snapcraft.io/t/classic-confinement-for-kontena-lens/13729/18)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:47
msgid ""
"[nautilus scripts](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/synchrorep-need-classic-"
"confinement/13347/8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:48
msgid "programming languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:49
msgid "public cloud agents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:50
msgid ""
"tools for local, non-root user driven configuration of/switching to "
"development workspaces/environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:51
msgid "terminal emulators, multiplexers and shells"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:52
msgid ""
"HPC or orchestration agents/software for running workloads on systems "
"without traditional users where the systems are otherwise managed outside of "
"the agent (ie, the software simply orchestrates running workloads on systems "
"and doesn't manage the systems themselves). Note: many HPC/orchestration "
"applications can run with strict confinement and classic should only be "
"granted if snapd does not support the specific use case (eg, the [need for "
"user accounting](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/request-for-classic-"
"confinement-slurm/18309/11))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:53
msgid ""
"Installer snaps for Ubuntu Flavors based on the official [ubuntu-flavor-"
"installer](https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-flavor-installer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:54
msgid ""
"AI agent/assistant that runs arbitrary user-directed code and needs to reach "
"files and programs that aren’t known at build time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:56
msgid "Unsupported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:57
msgid "management snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:58
msgid ""
"3rd party installer snaps (eg, for native packages, AppImages, Flatpaks, "
"Snaps, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:59
msgid "difficulty making strict confinement work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:60
msgid ""
"dependent software only available on host (ship in instead snap (eg, stage-"
"packages, build from source))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:61
msgid ""
"access to dot files in $HOME (use $HOME instead of getent*, personal-files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:62
msgid "access to /etc (use layouts, system-files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:63
msgid "hard-coded paths (use snapcraft-preload, layouts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:64
msgid "ability to run other snaps directly (as opposed to defined interfaces)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:65
msgid ""
"access to arbitrary files on the system because the application isn't "
"designed with confinement in mind (if a desktop application, use portals or "
"[xdg-open](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/allowing-xdg-open-to-open-files/"
"3789/11))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:66
msgid ""
"access to arbitrary files on the system due to developer/user inertia ({ref}"
"`home <interfaces-home-interface>` and {ref}`removable-media <interfaces-"
"removable-media-interface>` is almost always sufficient, though {ref}"
"`personal-files <interfaces-personal-files-interface>` and {ref}`system-"
"files <interfaces-system-files-interface>` may be used under certain "
"circumstances)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:67
msgid ""
"access to arbitrary files on the system to avoid increasing a snap's size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:68
msgid ""
"[GNOME shell extensions](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/yaru-dark-theme-toggle-"
"review-request/13169/7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:69
msgid ""
"[nautilus extensions](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/synchrorep-need-classic-"
"confinement/13347/8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:70
msgid ""
"access to [org.kde.PlasmaShell.evaluateScript](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/"
"issue-establishing-dbus-interface-with-org-kde-plasmashell/14908/4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:71
msgid ""
"access to [org.kde.klauncher5 (klauncher)](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/"
"18377) ([modify application](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/18377/3) to launch "
"programs directly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:72
msgid ""
"direct access to sudo (modify program (eg, check if root and if not, alert "
"user to run under sudo))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:73
msgid ""
"direct access to pkexec (modify program (eg, check if root and if not, alert "
"user to run under sudo; note a polkit backend is planned but not roadmapped, "
"so a snap may one day be able to use pkexec, but this is TBD))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:75
msgid "Criteria"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:76
msgid "This lists some criteria that might require classic (non-exhaustive):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:77
msgid "access to files on the host outside the snap's runtime (eg, /usr)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:78
msgid ""
"running arbitrary command (esp if user-configurable such as a developer tool "
"to organize dev environments)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:79
msgid ""
"access to resources not yet supported by snapd and where the requirement is "
"clearly understood to be supportable by snapd. This may result in "
"temporarily granting classic until snapd supports the use case in strict mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:81
msgid ""
"NOTE: while something may be known to require classic, that alone may not "
"justify granting classic confinement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:83
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:84
msgid ""
"Classic confinement sometimes might seem like the perfect solution to a "
"publisher's problem, but snaps that use `confinement: classic` differ from "
"strict mode snaps in important ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:86
msgid "they are not installable on Ubuntu Core (all snaps) devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:87
msgid ""
"they run in the global mount namespace (ie, the host's filesystem) as "
"opposed to what is specified by `base` in the snap's yaml."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:89
msgid ""
"Because of '2', great care must be taken for the snap to work reliably "
"across all distributions since, for example, as part of the build process "
"snapcraft will adjust the snap's binaries through binary patching and/or "
"setting environment variables to look into the `$SNAP` directory for paths, "
"either of which could affect the snap's reliability when running on "
"arbitrary cross-distribution host filesystems. In contrast, strict mode "
"snaps use what is specified by `base` in the snap's yaml as the basis for "
"its root filesystem at runtime and can depend on it not changing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:93
msgid "Additional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/reviewing-classic-confinement-snaps.md:94
msgid ""
"Sometimes it might make sense for a snap to be allowed the use of classic "
"(eg, for classic distro) but be usable in strict mode (eg, for Ubuntu Core). "
"In these cases, rather than having two separate snaps, it is considered best "
"to have [two separate tracks](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/new-track-classic-"
"request-for-the-nano-snap/10762/11), the default track and another called "
"`classicmode`."
msgstr ""
